A curried function shares its ambient context
sig f : () -> () -> () fun f()() {} f
stdout : fun : [] (() -> () -> ())
args : --set=show_quantifiers=true

An ambient callback shares the context of its caller
sig f : (() -> Int) -> Int fun f(g) { g() } f(fun() { 42 })
stdout : 42 : Int

A call with native permission
sig say : [wild] ((String) -> ()) fun say(s) { print(s) } say("hello")
stdout : @hello\s*\(\) : \(\)

A pure function cannot use native permission
sig say : [] ((String) -> ()) fun say(s) { print(s) } say("hello")
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

A relative callback supplies its handled effect
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig f : forall a::Abs. (<Reader> (() -> a)) -> a fun f(g) { handle(g()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(41) } } f(fun() { do Ask + 1 })
stdout : 42 : Int

An ambient callback cannot run in a handler's extended context
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig f : (() -> Int) -> Int fun f(g) { handle(g()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(41) } }
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

A fixed operation requirement needs the interface in scope
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig apply : ([Reader] (() -> Int)) -> Int fun apply(f) { f() }
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

A callback may use the surrounding context after adding an interface
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } effect Extra { Other : () => Int; } sig h : (<Reader> (() -> Int)) -> Int fun h(f) { handle(f()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(40) } } handle(h(fun() { do Ask + do Other })) { case <Other => k> -> k(2) }
stdout : 42 : Int

Braced record presence and absence
fun(r : (x{:Int}, y{-}, z{p}|e)) { r.x }
stdout : fun : ((x:Int,y-,z{_}|_)) -> Int

Absolute interface context
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } fun() { do Ask } : [Reader] (() -> Int)
stdout : fun : [Reader] (() -> Int)

An operation without an active instance cannot be invoked
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } effect Writer { Tell : () => Int; } fun() { do Tell } : [Reader] (() -> Int)
stderr : @.*Operation Tell requires effect interface Writer.*
exit : 1

Polymorphic nullary operation
effect Reader { Ask : forall a::Abs. () => a; } sig f : [Reader] (() -> Int) fun f(){ do Ask + 0 } f
stdout : fun : [Reader] (() -> Int)

Linear arrows can use native permission
linfun(x) { print(x); x } : [wild] ((String) -@ String)
stdout : fun : [wild] ((String) -@ String)

An empty context does not admit wild
fun() { print("hello") } : [] (() -> ())
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

Old wild arrows are rejected
fun() {} : () ~> ()
stderr : @.*Parse error:.*
exit : 1

Old effect arrows are rejected
fun() {} : () {Ask:Int}-> ()
stderr : @.*Parse error:.*
exit : 1

