A pure callback can run under an absolute requirement
sig pureCall : ([] (() -> Int)) -> Int fun pureCall(action) { action() } pureCall(fun() { 42 })
stdout : 42 : Int

A pure callback cannot use an enclosing handler's operations
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig pureCall : ([] (() -> Int)) -> Int fun pureCall(action) { action() } handle(pureCall(fun() { do Ask })) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) }
stderr : @.*Operation Ask requires effect interface Reader.*
exit : 1

A returned ambient function keeps its handled dependency
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } var delayed = handle(fun() { do Ask }) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) }; handle(delayed()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) }
stdout : 42 : Int

A returned ambient function requires the handled interface
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } var delayed = handle(fun() { do Ask }) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) }; delayed()
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

Transporting a callback through a handler cancels a mask
effect Tick { Tick : () => (); } sig hold : (() -> Int) -> () -> Int fun hold(f) { handle({ do Tick; (f : <Tick |>(() -> Int)) }) { case <Tick => k> -> k(()) } } hold(fun() { 42 })()
stdout : 42 : Int

A callback cannot be invoked with a masked interface
effect Tick { Tick : () => (); } sig hold : (() -> Int) -> Int fun hold(f) { handle({ do Tick; f() }) { case <Tick => k> -> k(()) } } hold(fun() { 42 })
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

A relative resumption needs a new handler
effect Next { Next : () => Int; } shallowhandle(do Next + do Next) { case <Next => k> -> k(20) }
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

An operation cannot be checked under a newly supplied absolute annotation
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } var bad = (do Ask : [Reader] Int); bad
stderr : @.*Operation Ask requires effect interface Reader.*
exit : 1

A handler must cover each operation of its interface
effect State(a::Abs) { Get : () => a; Put : (a) => (); } handle(handle({ do Put(true); do Get }) { case <Get => k> -> k(false) })(state <- 0) { case <Get => k> -> k(state, state) case <Put(n) => k> -> k((), n) }
stderr : @.*Incomplete handler for State.*Put.*
exit : 1

A handler can cover two complete interfaces
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } effect Choice { Choose : () => Bool; } handle(if (do Choose) do Ask else 0) { case <Choose => k> -> k(true) case <Ask => k> -> k(42) }
stdout : 42 : Int

An effectful global function needs a signature
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } fun ask() { do Ask }
stderr : @.*Operation Ask requires effect interface Reader.*
exit : 1

An inferred callback shares the enclosing handler's context
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } fun apply(f, x) { f(x) } handle(apply(fun(x) { x + do Ask }, 1)) { case <Ask => k> -> k(41) }
stdout : 42 : Int

An annotated function still needs its interface when called
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig ask : [Reader] (() -> Int) fun ask() { do Ask } ask()
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

An absolute result cannot be an ambient function
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig withAsk : forall a::Abs. (<Reader> (() -> a)) -> a fun withAsk(action) { handle(action()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) } } withAsk(fun() { fun() { do Ask } })
stderr : @.*Type argument .* must satisfy Abs.*
exit : 1

An absolute result cannot hold an ambient function in a record
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig withAsk : forall a::Abs. (<Reader> (() -> a)) -> a fun withAsk(action) { handle(action()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) } } withAsk(fun() { (run=fun() { do Ask }) })
stderr : @.*Type argument .* must satisfy Abs.*
exit : 1

An absolute function returned by a handler can run under a new handler
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } sig withAsk : forall a::Abs. (<Reader> (() -> a)) -> a fun withAsk(action) { handle(action()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) } } var f = withAsk(fun() { (fun() { do Ask } : [Reader] (() -> Int)) }); handle(f()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) }
stdout : 42 : Int

A conditional between values can introduce a modality
var f = (if (true) fun(x) { x } else fun(x) { x }) : [] ((Int) -> Int); f(42)
stdout : 42 : Int

An absolute operation payload cannot use an enclosing handler's operation
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } effect Runner { Run : ([] ((Int) -> Int)) => Int; } handle(handle(do Run(fun(x) { x + do Ask })) { case <Run(f) => k> -> k(f(40)) }) { case <Ask => k> -> k(2) }
stderr : @.*Operation Ask requires effect interface Reader.*
exit : 1

A higher-rank callback needs an annotation
fun ident(x) { x } fun both(f) { (f(42), f(true)) } both(~ident)
stderr : @.*Expected Int, got Bool.*
exit : 1

A higher-rank callback can use its argument at independently chosen types
sig ident : forall a. [] ((a) -> a) fun ident(x) { x } fun both(f : (forall a. [] ((a) -> a))) { (f(42), f(true)) } both(~ident)
stdout : (42, true) : (Int, Bool)

An absolute list function retains the list's element type
sig keepInts : [] ((List Int) -> List Int) fun keepInts(xs) { xs } keepInts([20, 22])
stdout : [20, 22] : List Int

A variant payload must match the declared type
typename MaybeInt = (| Nothing | Just:Int |); Just(true) : MaybeInt
stderr : @.*Expected Int, got Bool.*
exit : 1
